<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 27.55 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 27.55 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 18 basis points to 27.55 percent, but rates are seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of eight Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY	CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     27.37	    27.55		   + 18 bps</p>
<p>    90-DAY     26.85	    26.79		   -  6 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    25.62	    25.45		   - 17 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     25.68	    25.65		   -  3 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
</text>
